.TH CONVERTIBLE-HELPER 1 "October 2026" "convertible-helper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
convertible-helper \- tablet-mode and tablet-button helper for convertible laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convertible-helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B convertible-helper
runs as a systemd user service (convertible-helper.service) and uses only the
kernel's input events and mutter's org.gnome.Mutter.DisplayConfig D-Bus
interface. It watches every input device that has a tablet-mode switch, and the
Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 tablet button device.
.PP
When the laptop enters tablet mode it enables the on-screen keyboard setting
(org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications screen-keyboard-enabled) and restores the
previous value when tablet mode ends. When tablet mode ends it also sets the
built-in display back to normal orientation, after a 400 ms delay because the
switch can flicker while the screen is being turned.
.PP
The CF-19 rotation button (KEY_PROG3) rotates the built-in display one step
clockwise; the CF-19 "security" button (KEY_PROG1) opens the log-out dialog of
GNOME, Xfce or KDE.
.PP
The user must be able to read the input devices; the package's udev rule gives
that to the user on the seat through the "uaccess" tag.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-convertible-helper.rules
Access rule for the switch and button devices.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1)
(use
.B journalctl --user -u convertible-helper
for the log).
